Modern mobile browsers (and Replit previews) have aggressive security that often "kills" the sensor initialization before it even starts. Based on your screenshots showing
AUDIO_INIT_FAILED
, there are two specific blockers we need to bypass.
1. The "User Gesture" Requirement
Browsers like Chrome and Safari will block any
AudioContext
that is created automatically. It
must
be resumed or started by a physical tap on the screen. Even if you tap "Init," if the code isn't structured exactly right, the browser will ignore it.
2. The HTTPS/Secure Context Rule
navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia
(your microphone) is strictly disabled unless the site is running on a secure
https://
connection. If you are previewing in Replit, ensure you are using the
"Open in New Tab"
button (the small arrow icon at the top right of your preview) to ensure you are on a full SSL-secured page.
THE "FORCE_INITIALIZE" FIX
